.TH CSTRING_SET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_set \- replace the entire content with a new C string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

ccol_retval_t cstring_set(cstr s, const char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function throws away the current content of s and puts a copy of str
in its place. It grows the buffer when it has to, but it never shrinks
it.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to change
str   New content (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - The set succeeded
ccol_invalid_args         - str is NULL
ccol_container_full       - str is too large to represent. No real
                            program gets this code, since such a str
                            would need the whole address space
ccol_not_enough_memory    - The reallocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_reset (3),
.BR cstring_append (3)
